# Files in this repo that are NOT part of the published site.
#
# The assets directory is the repository root (same as Netlify's publish
# directory), so everything not listed here would be served. Cloudflare parses
# `_headers` even though it is listed below — verified against the deployed
# Dashboard Portal, which applies its CSP while serving no `/_headers` — so the
# header policy stays in effect without the file itself being readable.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.freebuff/
.wrangler/
.netlify/
node_modules/

netlify/
migrations/
tools/
brag-output/

# Local secrets for `wrangler dev` — the same file .gitignore refuses.
.dev.vars

README.md
CLAUDE.md
LICENSE
_headers
package.json
package-lock.json
wrangler.toml
.assetsignore
# The function half of the site. Pages compiles this directory at deploy time —
# a file here is a route, not an asset — and the upload is a staged copy of the
# repository, so without this rule the router and the catch-all would also be
# published as static files under /functions/.
functions/
# Deploy files: the script that stages the upload and the staging output it
# writes (`.pages-dist/`) are development files. The assets directory is the
# repository root, so anything not listed here would be uploaded and served.
.pages-dist/
